Subject: [PATCH 1/1] ms/seh: build the corpus against mingw-w64 headers

Delta applied to the vendored Microsoft SEH conformance corpus
(modules/rostests/apitests/compiler/ms/seh) so it compiles and links outside
the ReactOS SDK, against plain mingw-w64 headers. Two independent problems:

1. seh.h -- exception-info intrinsics.
   mingw-w64's excpt.h declares _exception_code/_exception_info/
   _abnormal_termination as ordinary functions (on MSVC they are intrinsics)
   and defines GetExceptionCode() and friends in terms of them. On a PSEH2
   build nothing defines those symbols, so every test that inspects an
   exception fails at link time with "undefined reference to _exception_code".
   Redirect them onto whichever backend pseh2.h selected. Guarded so that
   backends already providing them as macros (PSEH3, the amd64 GCC plugin)
   and native-SEH builds are untouched.

2. seh0020..seh0026 -- setjmp spelling.
   The corpus calls MSVC's one-argument _setjmp(jmp_buf). On mingw-w64
   _setjmp is not that function: it is usually a macro aliasing
   __intrinsic_setjmp, and the underlying routine takes a second argument (the
   establisher frame) that Win64 unwinding requires. Overriding _setjmp in the
   preprocessor only breaks mingw's own alias, so the call sites are rewritten
   to plain setjmp(), whose mingw macro already expands to the right spelling
   (_setjmp / _setjmp3 / _setjmpex / __mingw_setjmp) with the correct frame
   argument per architecture and CRT.

NOTE: this patch touches ONLY the test corpus. The PSEH implementation
(sdk/lib/pseh) and the GCC SEH plugin (sdk/tools/gcc_plugin_seh) are used
verbatim and are deliberately left unmodified, so that measured results
describe upstream PSEH as it actually ships.
---
diff --color -urN a/seh.h b/seh.h
--- a/seh.h	2026-08-29 12:16:09
+++ b/seh.h	2026-08-29 12:16:09
@@ -27,3 +27,31 @@
 #define gcc_volatile volatile
 
 #endif
+
+/* ---- ReactOS PSEH harness: mingw-w64 portability shims (added downstream) ----
+ *
+ * mingw-w64's excpt.h declares _exception_code / _exception_info /
+ * _abnormal_termination as real functions -- they are MSVC intrinsics -- and
+ * defines GetExceptionCode() & friends in terms of them. Nothing provides
+ * those symbols on a PSEH2 build, so every test that inspects an exception
+ * fails to link. Redirect them onto whichever backend pseh2.h selected.
+ * Backends that already define these as macros (PSEH3, the amd64 GCC plugin)
+ * are left alone by the guards.
+ */
+#if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(_SEH2_NATIVE_SEH)
+# undef GetExceptionCode
+# define GetExceptionCode() _SEH2_GetExceptionCode()
+# undef GetExceptionInformation
+# define GetExceptionInformation() _SEH2_GetExceptionInformation()
+# undef AbnormalTermination
+# define AbnormalTermination() _SEH2_AbnormalTermination()
+# if !defined(_abnormal_termination)
+#  define _abnormal_termination() _SEH2_AbnormalTermination()
+# endif
+# if !defined(_exception_code)
+#  define _exception_code() _SEH2_GetExceptionCode()
+# endif
+# if !defined(_exception_info)
+#  define _exception_info() _SEH2_GetExceptionInformation()
+# endif
+#endif
